The woman gives me a card.
"Here is your CPR number," she says.
Now I have a CPR number.
There are ten numbers on the card.
The first six numbers are my date of birth.
It is my personal number.
"The number is very important," the woman says.
"It is private, and you must take care of it."
I understand.
I look at the numbers.
They are my numbers now.
I put the card carefully in my bag.
Now I am in the system.
It is a big moment.
